    {
      "id": "bvddytb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11.2 Blockchain Technology"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i3k3wkx",
      "content": "Blockchain is a distributed, immutable ledger that records transactions across a network of computers. Each block contains a cryptographic hash of the previous block, timestamp, and transaction data, forming a chain."
    },
    {
      "id": "muk6ups",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Concept</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Description</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Distributed Ledger</p>",
            "<p>Copy of ledger maintained by all participants; no central authority</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Immutability</p>",
            "<p>Once recorded, data cannot be altered without consensus of network</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hash (SHA-256)</p>",
            "<p>Cryptographic function; each block contains hash of previous block — creates chain</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Consensus Mechanisms</p>",
            "<p>PoW (Proof of Work — Bitcoin; energy intensive), PoS (Proof of Stake — Ethereum 2.0), DPoS, PoA</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Smart Contracts</p>",
            "<p>Self-executing code on blockchain; trigger automatically when conditions met; Ethereum (Solidity)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Public Blockchain</p>",
            "<p>Open to all; permissionless; Bitcoin, Ethereum</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Private Blockchain</p>",
            "<p>Restricted access; permissioned; one organisation controls</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Consortium Blockchain</p>",
            "<p>Semi-private; multiple organisations share control</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hyperledger Fabric</p>",
            "<p>Enterprise private/consortium blockchain; used in banking, supply chain; IBM, Linux Foundation</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>CBDC (Central Bank Digital Currency)</p>",
            "<p>Digital currency issued by central bank; RBI's e-Rupee (retail + wholesale)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>DeFi (Decentralised Finance)</p>",
            "<p>Financial services on blockchain without intermediaries; lending, trading, yield farming</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "peimhrl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11.3 Internet of Things (IoT)"
    },
    {
      "id": "yswzedp",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Aspect</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Details</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Definition</p>",
            "<p>Network of physical devices embedded with sensors, software, connectivity to exchange data</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Architecture</p>",
            "<p>Edge devices → Gateway → Cloud/Fog → Application</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Protocols</p>",
            "<p>MQTT (lightweight publish-subscribe), CoAP, Zigbee, Z-Wave, LoRaWAN, NB-IoT</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Security Challenges</p>",
            "<p>Weak default passwords; unpatched firmware; large attack surface; resource-constrained devices</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Banking IoT Uses</p>",
            "<p>ATM monitoring, branch security, smart vaults, contactless payments, wearable payments</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Industrial IoT (IIoT)</p>",
            "<p>Manufacturing, agriculture monitoring, smart grid, predictive maintenance</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Edge Computing</p>",
            "<p>Process data near source (edge) rather than sending all to cloud; low latency; bandwidth efficient</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "23mlenw",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "11.4 Big Data Technologies"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Pay special attention to ML evaluation metrics such as Precision, Recall, F1-score, and ROC-AUC frequently asked in competitive technical exams.",
        "Understand fundamental concepts of Blockchain such as distributed ledgers, consensus algorithms, and smart contracts.",
        "Review CI/CD workflow automation, continuous integration stages, and continuous deployment practices under DevOps infrastructure."
      ],
      "id": "1fa9fjz"
    },
    {
      "id": "k3hqfy4",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Technology</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Category</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Purpose</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Features</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Hadoop (HDFS + MapReduce)</p>",
            "<p>Distributed Storage + Processing</p>",
            "<p>Process massive datasets on commodity hardware</p>",
            "<p>Write-once-read-many; NameNode + DataNode; MapReduce programming model</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Apache Spark</p>",
            "<p>In-memory Processing</p>",
            "<p>Fast batch + streaming analytics; replaces MapReduce</p>",
            "<p>100x faster than Hadoop; RDD, DataFrames; Spark SQL, MLlib, Streaming</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Apache Kafka</p>",
            "<p>Message Streaming</p>",
            "<p>High-throughput distributed message queue; real-time data pipelines</p>",
            "<p>Topics, Partitions, Producers, Consumers; Zookeeper/KRaft; used in fintech for real-time events</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Apache Hive</p>",
            "<p>Data Warehouse</p>",
            "<p>SQL-like queries on Hadoop (HiveQL); batch analytics</p>",
            "<p>Schema on read; partitioning; ORC/Parquet formats</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Apache HBase</p>",
            "<p>NoSQL Database on Hadoop</p>",
            "<p>Random read/write access to big data; column-family store</p>",
            "<p>Wide-column; scalable; used for time-series, event data in banking</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Elasticsearch</p>",
            "<p>Search + Analytics Engine</p>",
            "<p>Full-text search; log analytics; near real-time search</p>",
            "<p>Inverted index; JSON documents; ELK Stack (with Logstash + Kibana)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Apache Flink</p>",
            "<p>Stream Processing</p>",
            "<p>Real-time stateful stream processing; exactly-once semantics</p>",
            "<p>Lower latency than Spark Streaming; event-time processing; CEP</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
